{"id":201468448679897,"type":"album","name":"Will the Circle Be Unbroken","artist":"The Nitty Gritty Dirt Band","year":1972,"weight":37,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710705.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-f32b26ca-2868-4270-bcfd-c5a2614d2a75/mbid-f32b26ca-2868-4270-bcfd-c5a2614d2a75-11382982094.jpg","yt":"MvhoseYhhtc","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-nitty-gritty-dirt-band/will-the-circle-be-unbroken/"},"desc":"Will the Circle be Unbroken is the seventh album by the Nitty Gritty Dirt Band, with collaboration from many famous bluegrass and country-western players, including Roy Acuff, \"Mother\" Maybelle Carter, Doc Watson, Earl Scruggs, Randy Scruggs, Merle Travis, Pete \"Oswald\" Kirby, Norman Blake, Jimmy Martin, and others. It also introduced fiddler Vassar Clements to a wider audience. Every track on the album was recorded on the first or second take straight to two-track masters, so the takes are raw and unprocessed. Additionally, another tape ran continuously throughout the entire week-long recording session and captured the dialog between the players. On ."},"artist_ref":{"id":266769787282571,"name":"The Nitty Gritty Dirt Band","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Dirt_Band_1976.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":156823753286980,"type":"genre","name":"folk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":510,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":90510611927654,"type":"genre","name":"Country Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":425,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":239718708636602,"type":"genre","name":"Bluegrass","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":263,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":134533750493307,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Country","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":216,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":71665924433698,"type":"genre","name":"Appalachian Folk Music","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":201,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":90674871953462,"type":"genre","name":"Bluegrass Gosp